---
import ModuleWrapper, { type _ModuleWrapper, type _ModuleHeader } from "@/components/ui/modules/ModuleWrapper.astro";

export interface Props extends _ModuleWrapper {}

const props = Astro.props;

const header: _ModuleHeader = {
	...props.header,
	title: props.header?.title || "Education",
};
---

<ModuleWrapper {...{ ...props, header }}>
	<p>
		The real question behind a degree is whether I can deliver something I do not already know how to do yet. Every time a project handed me that, I took the time to learn it and then shipped it.
		Doing that on somebody's deadline is its own qualification, and it has been enough for a regulated Stockholm fintech and for a part-time CTO seat.
	</p>

	<p>
		What I do have is a Certificate III in Information Technology, earned across a twelve-month traineeship running a high school's network in 2008, and four qualifications from the International
		Coaching Institute between 2010 and 2011. The senior one of those is Advanced Practitioner of Executive and Leadership Coaching.
	</p>
</ModuleWrapper>
